@* Row-level component: the memoisation boundary sits at the ROW, not the cell.
   An unchanged row skips re-rendering entirely, while the cells inside stay plain
   markup so a full rebuild does not pay per-cell component overhead — 40
   boundaries instead of 800.

   The skip does NOT come for free. Blazor's automatic parameter change detection
   only reports "unchanged" for value/immutable-typed parameters; a mutable
   reference type such as Row is always treated as "may have changed", even when
   the reference is identical. So the boundary has to be enforced by hand in
   ShouldRender().

   Consequence worth carrying into the real design: identity, not mutation, is the
   change signal. A Consumer that mutates a row object in place will not repaint —
   it has to hand over a different instance, or bump Version.

   SelFrom/SelTo exist to price the "paint selection with per-cell classes"
   approach: selection is NOT part of the row's identity, so making it visible
   this way forces it into the parameter set and defeats the memoisation on every
   selection change. The overlay approach leaves these at -1 and never touches
   the row at all. *@

<div class="r">
    <div class="c key">@RowData.Book</div>
    @for (var c = 0; c < VisibleCols; c++)
    {
        var ci = c;
        var sel = ci >= SelFrom && ci <= SelTo;
        var value = Cols[ci].Get(RowData);
        var cls = Tone is null ? CellFormat.Class(Meta(RowData, ci)) : CellFormat.Class(Meta(RowData, ci), Tone(value));
        <div class="@(sel ? cls + " sel" : cls)">@CellFormat.Value(value)</div>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public Row RowData { get; set; } = default!;
    [Parameter] public Col[] Cols { get; set; } = [];
    [Parameter] public int VisibleCols { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public Func<Row, int, CellState> Meta { get; set; } = default!;
    /// <summary>The per-cell tone rule (RowComponentTone), or null for none. Cached by the
    /// parent for the same reason Meta is.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<object, CellTone>? Tone { get; set; }
    /// <summary>Bumped by the Consumer when a row's contents changed without changing identity.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int Version { get; set; }
    /// <summary>Selected column range within this row, or -1/-1 when selection is painted by an overlay.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int SelFrom { get; set; } = -1;
    [Parameter] public int SelTo { get; set; } = -1;

    private Row? _renderedRow;
    private Col[]? _renderedCols;
    private int _renderedVisibleCols = -1;
    private int _renderedVersion = -1;
    private int _renderedSelFrom = -2;
    private int _renderedSelTo = -2;

    protected override bool ShouldRender()
    {
        if (ReferenceEquals(_renderedRow, RowData)
            && ReferenceEquals(_renderedCols, Cols)
            && _renderedVisibleCols == VisibleCols
            && _renderedVersion == Version
            && _renderedSelFrom == SelFrom
            && _renderedSelTo == SelTo)
        {
            return false;
        }

        _renderedRow = RowData;
        _renderedCols = Cols;
        _renderedVisibleCols = VisibleCols;
        _renderedVersion = Version;
        _renderedSelFrom = SelFrom;
        _renderedSelTo = SelTo;
        return true;
    }
}
